    "data": {
      "title": "Postfix Calculator",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "tokens = input().split()\nvalues = []\n\nfor token in tokens:\n    if token in (\"+\", \"-\", \"*\"):\n        right = values.pop()\n        left = values.pop()\n\n        if token == \"+\":\n            result = left + right\n        elif token == \"-\":\n            result = left - right\n        else:\n            result = left * right\n    else:\n        result = int(token)\n\n    values.append(result)\n\nprint(values[0])\n",
      "statement": "Evaluate a valid <<postfix expression>> with integers and the operators {{+}}, {{-}} and {{*}}. Print its result. In postfix notation, each operator follows its two operands.\n\n<<Example:>> {{3 -5 + 10 4 - *}}\n<<Stack: bottom → top>>\n\n{{3}}: <<push>> {{3}} → {{[3]}}\n{{-5}}: <<push>> {{-5}} → {{[3, -5]}}\n{{+}}: <<pop>> {{-5}}, {{3}} → {{3 + (-5) = -2}} → <<push>> {{-2}} → {{[-2]}}\n{{10}}: <<push>> {{10}} → {{[-2, 10]}}\n{{4}}: <<push>> {{4}} → {{[-2, 10, 4]}}\n{{-}}: <<pop>> {{4}}, {{10}} → {{10 - 4 = 6}} → <<push>> {{6}} → {{[-2, 6]}}\n{{*}}: <<pop>> {{6}}, {{-2}} → {{-2 * 6 = -12}} → <<push>> {{-12}} → {{[-12]}}\n\n<<Output:>> {{-12}}\n\n<<Note:>> The first value popped is the right operand, so popping {{4}} before {{10}} gives {{10 - 4}}, not {{4 - 10}}.",
